msgid ""
"Now that we have the basics covered there are several options to look at for "
"your XR game dev journey:"
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que nous avons les bases couvertes il y a plusieurs options à "
"regarder pour voyage de développeur de jeux VR :"

msgid ""
"You can take a look at the :ref:`Advanced topics <openxr-advanced-topics>` "
"section."
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez regarder la section :ref:`Sujets avancés <openxr-advanced-"
"topics>`."

msgid ""
"You can look at a number of `XR demos here <https://github.com/godotengine/"
"godot-demo-projects/tree/master/xr>`_."
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez trouver de nombreux `projets de démo XR ici <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/xr>`_."

msgid ""
"You can find 3rd party tutorials on our :ref:`Tutorials and resources "
"<doc_community_tutorials>` page."
msgstr ""
"Sur notre page :ref:`Tutoriels et ressources <doc_community_tutorials>`, "
"vous trouverez des tutoriels de tierces partis."

msgid ""
"The vendor plugin isn't just for :ref:`deploying to Android "
"<doc_deploying_to_android>`. In the vendor plugin, we implement many OpenXR "
"vendor extensions that unlock unique features on certain devices, or "
"features that are new enough that a standardized implementation is not "
"available yet."
msgstr ""
"Le plugin fournisseur n'est pas seulement pour :ref:`déployer vers Android "
"<doc_deploying_to_android>`. Dans le plugin fournisseur, nous implémentons "
"de nombreuses extensions de fournisseurs OpenXR qui débloquent des "
"fonctionnalités uniques sur certains appareils, ou des fonctionnalités qui "
"sont suffisamment nouvelles pour qu'une implémentation normalisée ne soit "
"pas encore disponible."

msgid ""
"Together with the OpenXR working group we maintain a `client support matrix "
"<https://github.khronos.org/OpenXR-Inventory/"
"extension_support.html#client_matrix>`_ that lists all the OpenXR extensions "
"Godot supports and whether they require the vendor plugin."
msgstr ""
"Avec le groupe de travail OpenXR, nous maintenons une `matrice de support "
"client <https://github.khronos.org/OpenXR-Inventory/"
"extension_support.html#client_matrix>`_ qui répertorie toutes les extensions "
"OpenXR que Godot supporte et si elles nécessitent le plugin du fournisseur."

